## Lore

The Phlebus look almost exactly like humans; only a faint point to the
ears gives them away, and they can hide even that, because they can
reshape their faces and recolor their skin and hair at will. That gift
has put them high on the Coalition''s list of enemies of humanity as
likely spies, saboteurs and assassins, yet most Phlebus would rather use
it on a stage.

They are storytellers, actors, acrobats, jesters and showmen above all,
and even the adventurers among them never lose the urge to entertain. A
troupe of three once staged a whole classic play at a New Lazlo
playhouse, switching faces between scenes so fast that the audience
thought a dozen actors had performed. They are now among the most sought
after performers on the continent, found in the ''Burbs of Chi-Town, Lazlo,
Kingsdale, MercTown, the Magic Zone and many other places.

Nobody knows where they came from: their history is all spoken, and they
embroider every tale, which they see as showmanship rather than lying.
They claim to be fearless and will face most monsters boldly, but ghosts
and Entities terrify them, and they shun haunted places altogether.

## GM Notes

The book heads the race an optional player character or NPC.

Favoured O.C.C.s: Preacher, Rogue Scholar, Vagabond (leaning toward
entertainment), City Rat, Smuggler, Freelance Spy, Bandit/Con Artist,
Bounty Hunter, Deputy, Merc Soldier, Saloon Bum/Stoolie and
Barmaid/Bartender; snake-oil salesman, circus act and carnival barker
come easily to them.

Size 5 feet 6 inches to 6 feet 6 inches (1.7 to 2 m). Weight 100 to 220
pounds (45 to 99 kg). Life span 3D6+90 years; mature at 15; they mate for
life and families have at least four children. NPC experience level 1D6.
Pronounced FLEE-bus; also called Story Men and Shake Actors.

Habitat: all over North America, especially boomtowns and travelling
shows, thickest in the Midwest from Minnesota and Michigan to Lone Star.
Slave market value 2D4x1,000 credits.

Allies: they get on with nearly everyone, D-Bees and humans alike, even
demons, as long as someone will listen. Enemies: the Coalition States,
Free Quebec and anyone paranoid about shape-changing spies; Floopers,
Kraks and Fingertooth Carpetbaggers are friendly rivals; and, for no known
reason, they hate the Tundra Rangers of Canada as well as ghosts and
Entities.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'phlebus');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'phlebus';

